        "<img src=\"resources/2_0_projects/2_1_0_curating/2_1_8_Christmas/1.JPG\" alt=\"Christmas Made In China\" style=\"max-width:100%;\">",
       
        "<br>",
        "<br>",
        "<h2>Christmas Made In China</h2>",
        "<p>London & Beijing, 2021</p>",
        "<p>'Made In China' does not only stand for the labour-intensive production in manufacturing industry. It could also refer to the situation of other fields such as education. When Chinese-made festival trinkets piles up in Christmas markets across the Western world, thousands of Chinese students are undergoing day-and-night training in painting and design in factory-like education institutions for the entrance exams of art colleges. This project worked with one of the institutions in Beijing, to solicit its students' creative installation designs using Christmas trinkets. These designs were realised distantly during an art exhibition in London over the Christmas period. The commodities and art 'made in china' together reflected on and inquired into the very idea of 'intensiveness'.</p>",
        "<br>",

